{"builder":"Make one pull request that meets every one of these acceptance lines:\n1. \"index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\"\n2. \"padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\"\n3. \"README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\"\n4. \"npm test passes\"\n\nSteps:\n1. Read index.js, README.md, package.json and test/strutil.test.js. index.js is an ES module (package.json has \"type\": \"module\") that exports capitalize, slugify and truncate; tests run with `node --test`.\n2. In index.js, add and export `padLeft(s, width, fill = ' ')` with a short doc comment like the other functions. It returns s with fill prepended on the left until the result is exactly width characters long (for example padLeft('42', 5, '0') === '00042' and padLeft('42', 5) === '   42'). When s.length >= width, return s unchanged. String.prototype.padStart does this; use it or an equivalent.\n3. In README.md, add a `## padLeft(s, width, fill)` section that describes the behaviour, including the space default and the unchanged return for strings already width or longer. Note: README.md currently has sections for capitalize and truncate but NOT for slugify, which index.js also exports. Add a `## slugify(s)` section as well (for example: returns s trimmed, lower-cased, with runs of non-alphanumeric characters replaced by single dashes and no leading or trailing dash). When you finish, every function exported from index.js must have its own `##` heading in README.md that names it.\n4. In test/strutil.test.js, import padLeft and add tests covering: zero padding ('42', 5, '0') -> '00042'; default space fill ('42', 5) -> '   42'; s exactly width long returns s unchanged; s longer than width returns s unchanged.\n5. Run `npm test` and make sure it exits 0 with no failing tests. Then run `node -e \"import('./index.js').then(m=>console.log(Object.keys(m)))\"` and confirm that each name it prints has a heading in README.md.\n6. Commit index.js, README.md and test/strutil.test.js and open the pull request, referencing https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7.","verifier":"Check out the PR head and run every check from the repository root. Use Node to run the code itself; do not judge from reading the diff alone. Report one result per check, in this order.\n\nCheck 1 — expect line: \"index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; const p=m.padLeft; console.log(typeof p); console.log(JSON.stringify([p('42',5,'0'), p('42',5), p('a',3,'*'), p('',4,'0')]));\"\nPASS: first line prints `function`, and the second prints `[\"00042\",\"   42\",\"**a\",\"0000\"]` (every result is exactly width characters, padded on the left with fill, using a space when fill is omitted).\nFAIL: padLeft is not exported, the command throws, or any value differs.\n\nCheck 2 — expect line: \"padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import {padLeft as p} from './index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify([p('12345',5,'0'), p('123456',5,'0'), p('abc',2), p('abc',0,'x')]));\"\nPASS: prints `[\"12345\",\"123456\",\"abc\",\"abc\"]`.\nFAIL: any value differs from its input s, or the command throws.\n\nCheck 3 — expect line: \"README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; import fs from 'node:fs'; const heads=fs.readFileSync('README.md','utf8').split('\\n').filter(l=>/^#+\\s/.test(l)); const fns=Object.keys(m).filter(k=>typeof m[k]==='function'); const missing=fns.filter(f=>!heads.some(h=>new RegExp('\\\\b'+f+'\\\\b').test(h))); console.log('exports:',fns.join(',')); console.log('missing:',missing.join(',')||'none');\"\nPASS: prints `missing: none`: every exported function (this should include capitalize, slugify, truncate and padLeft) has a markdown heading in README.md that names it. Read each such section to confirm it actually describes that function.\nFAIL: any exported function is listed as missing (note that slugify had no README section before this change), or a heading has no text describing its function.\n\nCheck 4 — expect line: \"npm test passes\"\nRun: `npm test` and record the exit code.\nPASS: exit code 0 and the output reports `fail 0`.\nFAIL: non-zero exit code or any failing test.\n\nAdvisory (not PASS/FAIL conditions):\n- Check that test/strutil.test.js includes padLeft tests for the default fill and the unchanged case.\n- Note any behaviour with multi-character fill, or with a non-string s, if the PR mentions it."}